      "question": "A curve has equation y = f(x). The point P(4, 32/3) lies on the curve. Given f''(x) = 4/sqrt(x) - 3 and f'(x) = 5 at P, find the equation of the tangent to the curve at P in the form y = mx + c.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "y = 5x - 28/3",
      "steps": [
        "Integrate f''(x) = 4x^(-1/2) - 3: f'(x) = 8x^(1/2) - 3x + A.",
        "At P (x = 4), f'(4) = 5: 16 - 12 + A = 5, so A = 1.",
        "So the gradient at P is m = 5.",
        "Tangent: y - 32/3 = 5(x - 4), so y = 5x - 20 + 32/3.",
        "Therefore y = 5x - 28/3."
      ]
